WEBVTT


00:00:30.648 --> 00:00:32.088
The question of happiness


00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:34.213
has preoccupied
philosophers, poets


00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:36.932
and pharmaceutical companies
for thousands of years.


00:00:38.088 --> 00:00:40.608
Clearly, it's a tricky one.


00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.528
When I graduated from
design school three years ago,


00:00:43.687 --> 00:00:46.415
I had a definite plan.


00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:50.168
Couple months at home,
put together a kickass portfolio,


00:00:50.327 --> 00:00:53.371
then I'd take Manhattan
by storm.


00:00:55.726 --> 00:00:57.287
And here is home.


00:00:58.287 --> 00:00:59.727
West Orange, New Jersey.


00:00:59.886 --> 00:01:01.491
Nice, huh?


00:01:03.087 --> 00:01:06.207
OK, it's not Manhattan,
but, like I say, it's temporary.


00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:10.130
I grew up here
with two families.


00:01:10.286 --> 00:01:12.970
That's my dad in blue,
and that's his best friend, Terry.


00:01:13.126 --> 00:01:14.970
The Inseparables.


00:01:15.126 --> 00:01:18.214
They go jogging together
three times a week without fail.


00:01:18.365 --> 00:01:20.526
You can set your clock by it.


00:01:20.685 --> 00:01:23.446
You could say life in the Oranges
is dependable.


00:01:23.605 --> 00:01:25.569
I can't believe
you made me do this.


00:01:25.725 --> 00:01:28.453
Good for your appetite.
See you in an hour.


00:01:28.605 --> 00:01:31.693
You can depend on Terry
to have a gadget for everything.


00:01:31.845 --> 00:01:34.572
Walked 1.2 miles.
Only stopped twice.


00:01:34.724 --> 00:01:36.045
That's great, honey.


00:01:36.204 --> 00:01:38.091
And you can
depend on Cathy


00:01:38.244 --> 00:01:40.044
to never hear
a single word he says.


00:01:40.204 --> 00:01:41.884
Make sure you put your bicycle
in the garage.


00:01:42.044 --> 00:01:43.888
And pull the pork
out of the freezer, honey.


00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:49.251
Across the street,
our house.


00:01:49.404 --> 00:01:51.771
Every year,
my mom gets more involved


00:01:51.924 --> 00:01:53.287
with her carolling group.


00:01:53.444 --> 00:01:55.244
They start rehearsing
in August.


00:01:55.403 --> 00:01:56.963
# Jingle bells
Jingle all the way... #


00:01:57.123 --> 00:01:59.688
And every year, my dad
hates them a little bit more.


00:02:02.723 --> 00:02:06.564
OK, sure. I'm still here.
I'm a few years behind in my plan.


00:02:06.723 --> 00:02:08.490
But you can't
rush these things.


00:02:08.643 --> 00:02:11.491
Portfolios need
to be perfect, right?


00:02:11.642 --> 00:02:14.282
Plus I have a day job
working in furniture, so...


00:02:14.442 --> 00:02:17.802
...as far as I was concerned,
everything was on track.


00:02:17.962 --> 00:02:21.006
# Happy birthday to you... #


00:02:21.161 --> 00:02:24.009
That is, until what
happened... happened


00:02:24.162 --> 00:02:26.246
Nina Ostroff.


00:02:26.401 --> 00:02:29.085
When all this started,
she was at a safe distance,


00:02:29.241 --> 00:02:31.281
3, 000 miles away
in San Francisco.


00:02:31.441 --> 00:02:35.085
I Happy birthday to you. I


00:02:35.241 --> 00:02:37.565
Make a wish, babe.


00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:47.208
And I was the fifth wheel


00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:49.608
to our parents'
regular Saturday foursome.


00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.440
Say it again.


00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:52.887
OK.


00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.363
Un coup de birch.


00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.003
Hey, Vanny.


00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.643
I read the most
interesting article


00:02:58.799 --> 00:03:00.567
called 'The IKEA Conspiracy',


00:03:00.719 --> 00:03:02.324
which you'd be
really fascinated by.


00:03:02.479 --> 00:03:03.800
- What it imagines is a...
- Terry?


00:03:03.959 --> 00:03:05.442
We need to call Nina.
We said 9:30.


00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:07.039
I'm on it.


00:03:07.199 --> 00:03:09.403
Vanessa, did you look at
that one-bedroom in Fort Lee?


00:03:09.558 --> 00:03:12.723
Yeah. It was, um, like a closet
in the basement.


00:03:12.878 --> 00:03:14.242
There's always something, honey.


00:03:14.398 --> 00:03:15.719
Don't be so choosy.
Nothing's perfect.


00:03:15.878 --> 00:03:18.039
There was, you know,
one window.


00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.042
- Paige, did I tell you...
- No room to breathe.


00:03:20.198 --> 00:03:21.878
...that Joan Marshack
was the listing agent on that?


00:03:22.038 --> 00:03:24.842
David, you are going
to really love this.


00:03:24.998 --> 00:03:29.799
This speaker box communicates
wirelessly with my cell phone.


00:03:29.958 --> 00:03:32.042
And guess where
I read about it first.


00:03:32.197 --> 00:03:34.205
'Consumer Reports'. Thank you
so much for the subscription.


00:03:34.358 --> 00:03:36.606
- I'm really enjoying it.
- You are consumingly welcome.


00:03:36.757 --> 00:03:39.845
I don't even have to take
my cell phone out of my pocket.


00:03:39.997 --> 00:03:41.318
Watch.


00:03:41.477 --> 00:03:43.321
Dial Nina.


00:03:43.477 --> 00:03:44.917
Please repeat request.


00:03:45.076 --> 00:03:46.397
Dial Nina.


00:03:46.557 --> 00:03:48.641
Maybe your pants
are blocking the signal.


00:03:48.796 --> 00:03:50.236
They're cotton.


00:03:51.676 --> 00:03:54.316
Nina's cell phone, dialling.


00:03:56.116 --> 00:03:59.117
Nina - their daughter
and my best friend


00:03:59.276 --> 00:04:01.284
from ages 0
to high school.


00:04:01.436 --> 00:04:03.836
We spent hours together
planning our big escape.


00:04:03.996 --> 00:04:05.960
I'm gonna live in New York.


00:04:06.115 --> 00:04:07.436
And Paris.


00:04:07.595 --> 00:04:09.843
And I'm gonna be a famous chef
and have a million lovers


00:04:09.995 --> 00:04:11.316
who'll take me
all over the world


00:04:11.475 --> 00:04:13.603
so I never have to come back
to New Jersey again.


00:04:13.755 --> 00:04:16.482
It's like
there's no air here, right?


00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:18.239
Totally.


00:04:20.914 --> 00:04:22.355
You'll come too, right?


00:04:22.514 --> 00:04:24.434
Are you kidding?


00:04:25.635 --> 00:04:27.402
Until sophomore year,


00:04:27.554 --> 00:04:31.842
when she abandoned me for
Liz Gaines and the Fun Bunch.


00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:38.634
She also kissed and later gave
a hand job to Peter Fortunate.


00:04:38.794 --> 00:04:41.914
I'd been secretly
in love with him forever.


00:04:43.033 --> 00:04:44.997
Then, just as her parents
were lining her up


00:04:45.153 --> 00:04:46.953
at some lame college
in Pennsylvania,


00:04:47.113 --> 00:04:49.557
she decided she was
going to travel the world.


00:04:49.713 --> 00:04:52.157
Or at least those parts


00:04:52.312 --> 00:04:54.232
that were out of
her mothefs cell phone range.


00:04:57.632 --> 00:04:59.279
Hello?


00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.832
Happy birthday, sweetie!


00:05:01.992 --> 00:05:03.640
- Happy birthday!
- Happy birthday, Nina.


00:05:03.792 --> 00:05:06.640
It's David and Paige.
Vanessa's here too.


00:05:06.792 --> 00:05:08.516
It's true. I'm here.


00:05:08.672 --> 00:05:09.960
Hey, Ethan.


00:05:10.111 --> 00:05:12.839
I think Nina's fucking parents
are on the phone.


00:05:14.592 --> 00:05:17.036
I didn't know I was having
a party. It was a surprise.


00:05:17.191 --> 00:05:19.275
Honey, we can't hear you.


00:05:19.431 --> 00:05:22.038
Ethan threw me
a surprise party.


00:05:22.191 --> 00:05:23.915
It's so great.


00:05:24.071 --> 00:05:25.392
Did you guys get
the pictures I sent?


00:05:25.551 --> 00:05:27.275
Yes, we did.


00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.111
More young men should have earrings
in their face.


00:05:29.271 --> 00:05:31.671
What? I'm sorry, I can't
hear you. Am I on speaker?


00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:35.551
Nina, what day are you
flying in for Thanksgiving?


00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:38.754
Thanksgiving. Mom, um...


00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:42.754
Uh, I don't think I'm gonna
make it for Thanksgiving.


00:05:42.909 --> 00:05:46.030
Ethan's photography show's
next weekend, and it's a big deal.


00:05:46.189 --> 00:05:47.989
Sweetie, we haven't
seen you for two years.


00:05:48.149 --> 00:05:49.513
You haven't been home
in five years.


00:05:49.669 --> 00:05:51.394
Since we visited you.
That's a long time.


00:05:51.549 --> 00:05:52.869
Um...


00:05:53.029 --> 00:05:55.037
Can you take me
off speaker, please?


00:05:55.189 --> 00:05:56.630
Sorry, sweetie,
I'd have to disconnect you


00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:58.753
to take you off speaker -
it's a very complex system.


00:05:58.909 --> 00:05:59.913
OK.


00:06:01.308 --> 00:06:04.157
Look, you're not
gonna like this, but...


00:06:04.308 --> 00:06:06.392
Ethan and I
are getting married.


00:06:06.548 --> 00:06:09.669
He proposed two weeks ago
on his birthday.


00:06:09.828 --> 00:06:11.432
He took me out
to Baker Beach,


00:06:11.588 --> 00:06:12.908
which overlooks
the Golden Gate Bridge,


00:06:13.068 --> 00:06:14.912
and he got down on one knee
and everything.


00:06:15.068 --> 00:06:18.472
- He proposed on his birthday?
- I don't understand.


00:06:18.628 --> 00:06:20.395
I'm in love with him.


00:06:21.388 --> 00:06:23.396
That's really great,
sweetie, but...


00:06:23.547 --> 00:06:25.588
You're only 24 years old.


00:06:25.747 --> 00:06:27.591
Nobody gets married
at 24 anymore.


00:06:27.747 --> 00:06:29.591
People get married
when they're 17.


00:06:29.747 --> 00:06:31.111
Not white girls
from New Jersey.


00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:32.827
- Shh!
- Would you listen to yourself?


00:06:32.987 --> 00:06:34.591
No, you listen -
you have made some


00:06:34.746 --> 00:06:36.950
very questionable decisions
in your life.


00:06:37.106 --> 00:06:38.470
Please don't
add to the list


00:06:38.626 --> 00:06:42.315
by marrying some loser kid
with zero future.


00:06:42.466 --> 00:06:45.434
OK. I have an idea.


00:06:45.586 --> 00:06:49.634
If you think he's such a loser,
then don't come to the wedding!


00:06:54.065 --> 00:06:55.745
Jesus, turn that thing down!


00:06:58.105 --> 00:07:02.546
Down volume!
Down volume!


00:07:02.705 --> 00:07:05.945
- Oh, God!
- Down volume!


00:07:11.865 --> 00:07:15.105
You guys, it's getting late.
The party's over, OK?


00:07:15.264 --> 00:07:17.032
Love you. 'Bye.


00:07:17.184 --> 00:07:18.668
Amy, did you see Ethan?


00:07:19.824 --> 00:07:21.265
Baby?


00:07:21.424 --> 00:07:23.584
Ethan?


00:07:27.543 --> 00:07:28.951
Ethan?


00:07:29.103 --> 00:07:31.427
Uh, it's...
Gimme a sec.


00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:33.951
Come on. I want to
get everybody out of here.


00:07:48.222 --> 00:07:50.262
Hey, how's it going with
the, uh, couples counsellor?


00:07:50.422 --> 00:07:52.986
I don't know.
She's so non-specific.


00:07:53.142 --> 00:07:55.782
It's like talking to fog.


00:07:55.942 --> 00:07:58.102
David and I know
where we stand with each other.


00:07:58.261 --> 00:08:00.629
That's how we've lasted this long.
Somehow, it works.


00:08:00.782 --> 00:08:04.306
Well, don't look at me.
I just pretend Terry's invisible.


00:08:04.461 --> 00:08:06.981
- Notice anything different?
- I sure do.


00:08:07.141 --> 00:08:08.865
Nice new mini fridge.


00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.462
I think it really
ties the room together.


00:08:10.621 --> 00:08:13.065
-It's the Max 5950.
-It's the one you recommended.


00:08:13.221 --> 00:08:15.108
From the patio series.
Good move.


00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.301
Let's take a look
in the mini ice compartment.


00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:20.500
Oh, boy.
It's really big, isn't it?


00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:23.748
Now, this stuff is huge
in Europe.


00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:26.387
And we've just landed
the American campaign.


00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.100
- No kidding? Congrats.
- Thanks.


00:08:28.259 --> 00:08:30.267
Russians like it
for breakfast.


00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:34.667
Before the devil
knows you're dead.


00:08:38.019 --> 00:08:39.786
Boy, it's, um...


00:08:39.939 --> 00:08:41.466
Well...
Really not very good, is it?


00:08:41.619 --> 00:08:43.463
-It's not good at all. No.
- No.


00:08:49.059 --> 00:08:50.542
What's up
with these sheets?


00:08:51.858 --> 00:08:53.899
You, um...


00:08:54.058 --> 00:08:55.858
...spending a little extra time
out here?


00:08:56.018 --> 00:08:58.179
Just a couple of nights a week.


00:08:58.338 --> 00:09:00.706
Late-night TV.


00:09:24.617 --> 00:09:27.421
You've gotta be
fucking kidding me.


00:09:34.416 --> 00:09:36.456
Oh, sh...


00:09:48.775 --> 00:09:50.302
Nina? Wow!


00:09:50.455 --> 00:09:53.259
- David. Hi.
- It's been so long.


00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:57.455
I thought you weren't
coming back for Thanksgiving.


00:09:57.615 --> 00:09:59.502
Yeah, well...


00:09:59.654 --> 00:10:01.422
Um...


00:10:02.974 --> 00:10:06.139
Are my parents here?
Locked out.


00:10:06.294 --> 00:10:08.542
They're in the back.


00:10:08.694 --> 00:10:11.334
Last day of barbecue season.


00:10:13.773 --> 00:10:16.054
What's going on?


00:10:16.213 --> 00:10:17.817
- You OK?
- David?


00:10:17.973 --> 00:10:20.373
Paige wants to know what
you did with the tong thing.


00:10:21.773 --> 00:10:23.453
Hi, Mom.


00:10:23.613 --> 00:10:26.733
I'm back for Thanksgiving.


00:10:26.892 --> 00:10:29.053
We turned it into
a second den.


00:10:29.212 --> 00:10:30.860
If your father's
in the first den


00:10:31.012 --> 00:10:32.572
and I want some privacy,
I come here.


00:10:32.733 --> 00:10:34.096
Honey,
I have this really cool


00:10:34.253 --> 00:10:35.573
self-inflating mattress.


00:10:35.732 --> 00:10:38.297
It fits perfectly in the corner
and it is really comfy.


00:10:40.692 --> 00:10:43.180
But, you know, we have your
old bed frame out there in the...


00:10:43.332 --> 00:10:45.219
...in the garage -
I can set it up for you.


00:10:45.372 --> 00:10:47.500
- Take me two...two se...
- No, that's fine.


00:10:47.651 --> 00:10:49.571
I'll only be here
a few days.


00:10:49.731 --> 00:10:52.176
Why? Where are you
going to now?


00:10:52.331 --> 00:10:54.776
I don't know.


00:10:56.531 --> 00:10:58.451
I haven't figured it out yet.


00:10:58.611 --> 00:11:00.498
Well, why don't you
stay here for a while?


00:11:00.650 --> 00:11:02.091
I don't care -
it's not like we haven't


00:11:02.251 --> 00:11:04.412
gotten used
to you being gone.


00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:07.010
Can you hold off
on the guilt trips


00:11:07.171 --> 00:11:08.491
for just a little while,
please?


00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:10.211
I've had
a rough couple days.


00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:14.730
I'd never seen Nina
with her tail between her legs.


00:11:14.889 --> 00:11:17.530
But I didn't
have time to gloat.


00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:20.734
Back on our side of the street,
we had our own problems.


00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:22.254
That's not what I'm saying.


00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.374
- What about Christmas?
- Come on, Paige.


00:11:24.529 --> 00:11:27.650
- I'm trying here.
- Oh. Now I'm not trying.


00:11:28.889 --> 00:11:30.536
Can't we have
a simple conversation?


00:11:30.689 --> 00:11:34.573
- I make one suggestion...
- I don't want to go down there.


00:11:34.729 --> 00:11:37.490
- You seem oblivious...
- Come on, Paige...


00:11:44.488 --> 00:11:46.736
I apologise
for what I said about Ethan.


00:11:46.888 --> 00:11:49.649
- Were you waiting for me?
- I'm not your enemy. Nina!


00:11:49.808 --> 00:11:51.292
When you're a parent
some day,


00:11:51.448 --> 00:11:52.856
you'll understand
what it feels like


00:11:53.007 --> 00:11:54.807
to have your child hate you.


00:11:55.848 --> 00:11:57.735
In case you're wondering,
that's your cue to say,


00:11:57.887 --> 00:11:59.208
"I don't hate you, Mom."


00:11:59.367 --> 00:12:00.775
I don't hate you.


00:12:00.927 --> 00:12:05.652
I just get furious
thinking someone has hurt you.


00:12:09.287 --> 00:12:12.691
Don't think I'm crazy.
This is just a thought. But, uh...


00:12:14.087 --> 00:12:16.454
Toby's coming home
for Thanksgiving.


00:12:18.206 --> 00:12:20.727
- Oh, my God.
- He's gotten very attractive.


00:12:20.886 --> 00:12:22.249
That's all I'm saying.


00:12:22.406 --> 00:12:24.326
He works for
the Federal Trade Commission.


00:12:24.486 --> 00:12:25.849
Terrific. You date him.


00:12:26.006 --> 00:12:27.806
Well, it's not like you two
don't have history.


00:12:27.966 --> 00:12:29.494
- We kissed!
- Yeah.


00:12:29.645 --> 00:12:30.966
Once, like, 10 years ago.


00:12:31.125 --> 00:12:33.569
Can you at least let me unpack
before pimping me out?


00:12:33.726 --> 00:12:36.410
OK, fine. But I'm gonna
tell you this for your own good.


00:12:36.565 --> 00:12:39.369
You need to have a real
relationship with a real man.


00:12:39.525 --> 00:12:41.969
It's time you grew up already!
Stop running away.


00:12:42.124 --> 00:12:45.125
You know, you're right.
I'm being selfish.


00:12:45.284 --> 00:12:46.725
The best thing
I can do right now


00:12:46.885 --> 00:12:48.205
is fulfil
your insane suburban fantasy


00:12:48.364 --> 00:12:49.685
where I marry
your best friend's son.


00:12:49.844 --> 00:12:53.249
Now, you go call the catering hall
and I'll lube my vagina.


00:12:53.404 --> 00:12:55.848
That was uncalled for.


00:12:56.004 --> 00:12:57.487
Uh, there's 12 of us
in the delegation.


00:12:57.644 --> 00:12:59.204
I'm really just...
just assisting my boss.


00:12:59.364 --> 00:13:01.328
But the goal is to
tie our trade agreements


00:13:01.483 --> 00:13:03.251
to stricter
environmental regulations


00:13:03.403 --> 00:13:05.531
since things
are kind of a mess over there.


00:13:06.923 --> 00:13:09.487
- China. That's great.
- Yeah, thanks.


00:13:09.643 --> 00:13:11.443
You are gonna have
a great experience.


00:13:11.603 --> 00:13:13.926
- Yeah. Yeah.
- It's, like, a 30-hour flight.


00:13:14.083 --> 00:13:16.123
- Honey, what about Christmas?
- Don't worry, Mom.


00:13:16.282 --> 00:13:17.603
I fly back on the 24th.


00:13:17.762 --> 00:13:19.290
That sounds
really great, Toby.


00:13:19.442 --> 00:13:22.203
I hear that ultimate frisbee
is exploding over there.


00:13:22.362 --> 00:13:24.446
In China. The, uh...


00:13:24.603 --> 00:13:28.084
The Beijing club team
came in second at the World's.


00:13:28.242 --> 00:13:29.846
If I see a game,
I'll let 'em know


00:13:30.002 --> 00:13:33.045
I grew up across the street
from the guy who invented it.


00:13:33.202 --> 00:13:36.770
Well. It wasn't just me. It was
also Jared Kass and, uh...


00:13:36.922 --> 00:13:38.569
- Honey?
- Joel Silver.


00:13:38.722 --> 00:13:40.326
Of course, Joel gets
most of the, you know...


00:13:40.481 --> 00:13:43.166
...most of the play, being
a big movie producer and all.


00:13:43.321 --> 00:13:45.569
Finally!


00:13:48.001 --> 00:13:50.129
Where there's dessert,
there's hope.


00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:57.521
Your mom told me about what
happened with that Ethan guy.


00:13:57.680 --> 00:13:59.600
You OK?


00:14:03.080 --> 00:14:04.400
Yeah.


00:14:04.560 --> 00:14:06.688
I'm good, thanks.


00:14:07.999 --> 00:14:09.919
So, what about you?


00:14:10.079 --> 00:14:12.088
How's the liquor
advertising business going?


00:14:12.239 --> 00:14:14.007
Still pushing booze
onto minors?


00:14:14.159 --> 00:14:16.603
Yes, I am.


00:14:16.759 --> 00:14:18.079
Actually,
I just got a promotion.


00:14:18.239 --> 00:14:19.766
I'm now executive
vice-president,


00:14:19.919 --> 00:14:21.239
creative accounts.


00:14:21.398 --> 00:14:22.926
Congratulations.


00:14:23.079 --> 00:14:25.207
Was that something
you wanted?


00:14:25.358 --> 00:14:27.399
Not really.


00:14:27.558 --> 00:14:29.478
You want me to spoon this
onto the plates?


00:14:29.638 --> 00:14:31.122
Please.


00:14:31.278 --> 00:14:34.759
Uh... Don't just eat it
right out the carton.


00:14:37.478 --> 00:14:40.358
Is it good?


00:14:42.557 --> 00:14:43.965
- It's cold.
- What?


00:14:44.118 --> 00:14:48.122
Hey. I brought that ice-cream
for the pies.


00:14:48.277 --> 00:14:50.164
He made me eat it.


00:14:51.397 --> 00:14:53.165
Well, Cathy wants
to serve dessert.


00:14:53.317 --> 00:14:55.085
Will you please
bring in some plates?


00:14:57.356 --> 00:14:59.724
I still need Christmas lists
from everyone by tonight.


00:14:59.877 --> 00:15:01.197
I'm leaving early tomorrow.


00:15:01.356 --> 00:15:03.364
- Black Friday.
- Don't make fun.


00:15:03.516 --> 00:15:07.324
Last year, I got there at 3am
and I was still 210 in line.


00:15:07.476 --> 00:15:08.916
Why would anyone
want to shop


00:15:09.076 --> 00:15:10.681
on the same day
as everyone else?


00:15:10.836 --> 00:15:12.756
I hear that
they have fist fights


00:15:12.916 --> 00:15:14.640
and people throw their children
at each other.


00:15:14.796 --> 00:15:17.644
Terry! No.
It's really a very...


00:15:17.795 --> 00:15:21.679
Very communal, Christmassy
experience. It's beautiful.


00:15:21.835 --> 00:15:23.199
Listen, I know it's late,


00:15:23.355 --> 00:15:24.839
but I think
we should have a toast.


00:15:24.995 --> 00:15:27.363
It's Thanksgiving. We have
so much to be thankful for.


00:15:27.515 --> 00:15:29.675
Toby is going to China.


00:15:29.834 --> 00:15:31.155
Very exciting.


00:15:31.315 --> 00:15:33.879
Nina is finally
back at home.


00:15:34.035 --> 00:15:36.796
And Vanessa
continues to live among us,


00:15:36.954 --> 00:15:38.634
bringing us joy every day.


00:15:38.794 --> 00:15:40.681
To the Walling
and Ostroff clans.


00:15:40.834 --> 00:15:44.402
Who knew that two families
could get this close?


00:15:44.554 --> 00:15:45.874
Hear, hear.


00:15:46.033 --> 00:15:48.598
I still think we could be
a little closer.


00:15:50.593 --> 00:15:52.874
Well said.


00:15:54.913 --> 00:15:58.001
Man, I thought your mom
was going to applaud


00:15:58.153 --> 00:15:59.474
when she saw us
leave together.


00:15:59.633 --> 00:16:02.481
The woman
is a total lunatic.


00:16:02.633 --> 00:16:04.477
In the first three years
I was gone,


00:16:04.633 --> 00:16:06.433
she sent me
letters from the cat.


00:16:06.592 --> 00:16:08.840
"Dear Nina,
Don't be difficult.


00:16:08.993 --> 00:16:10.400
"Call your mother
on her birthday."


00:16:10.552 --> 00:16:12.920
That's great, actually.
I kind of like that.


00:16:13.072 --> 00:16:15.560
Now you understand
why I never came back.


00:16:16.592 --> 00:16:18.675
Yeah. No, I hear ya. But...


00:16:18.832 --> 00:16:21.352
I'm glad you did.


00:16:22.671 --> 00:16:23.719
Shut up.


00:16:27.871 --> 00:16:29.595
Dance with me.


00:16:31.231 --> 00:16:32.715
Totally.


00:16:36.391 --> 00:16:37.951
You OK?


00:16:38.110 --> 00:16:39.431
I need to get some water.


00:16:39.591 --> 00:16:41.478
- Can I get some water?
- OK. Sit down, wild man.


00:16:41.631 --> 00:16:45.112
I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.


00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:51.954
- Hey.
- Toby needs water.


00:16:52.109 --> 00:16:53.877
What are you doing up?


00:16:54.029 --> 00:16:57.237
Just watching a little TV
in the man cave.


00:16:57.390 --> 00:17:00.510
- Man cave?
- It's the pool house.


00:17:00.669 --> 00:17:03.430
I got one of those
worldwide sports...


00:17:03.589 --> 00:17:05.717
...something something package
your dad recommended.


00:17:05.869 --> 00:17:08.073
There's this
Korean basketball league


00:17:08.229 --> 00:17:09.876
which is completely crazy.


00:17:10.029 --> 00:17:12.157
You know, it's not good
to eat peanut butter


00:17:12.308 --> 00:17:13.629
this late at night.


00:17:13.788 --> 00:17:15.109
It'll make you fat.


00:17:15.268 --> 00:17:17.112
I'm not fat.


00:17:17.268 --> 00:17:18.993
You will be if you
keep eating like that


00:17:19.148 --> 00:17:20.468
at 2:00 in the morning.


00:17:20.628 --> 00:17:22.275
And where'd you pick
this little factoid up?


00:17:22.428 --> 00:17:24.032
I worked in
a lot of restaurants.


00:17:24.187 --> 00:17:26.315
Restaurants
that serve peanut butter?


00:17:26.468 --> 00:17:28.476
Look, do whatever you want.


00:17:28.628 --> 00:17:31.072
I'm just saying
that you wouldn't look good fat.


00:17:33.547 --> 00:17:35.434
I should get back downstairs.


00:17:35.587 --> 00:17:37.354
Yeah, make your mother
very happy. You know that.


00:17:37.507 --> 00:17:38.827
It's what I live for.


00:18:26.224 --> 00:18:28.144
- Hi.
- Hi.


00:18:29.344 --> 00:18:30.871
What happened to Toby?


00:18:31.024 --> 00:18:32.944
I cut him up
in little pieces


00:18:33.104 --> 00:18:34.904
and put him in the fridge
for later.


00:18:42.103 --> 00:18:43.663
Who's playing?


00:18:45.263 --> 00:18:47.107
I have no idea.


00:18:47.263 --> 00:18:49.107
It's...it's the, um...


00:18:51.463 --> 00:18:53.546
...guys in red against the...
the guys in white.


00:18:53.703 --> 00:18:55.350
- White. I got it.
- Yeah. Yeah.


00:18:55.503 --> 00:18:57.511
Go, reds.


00:18:57.662 --> 00:18:59.343
Or White.


00:18:59.502 --> 00:19:01.182
You know.


00:19:44.899 --> 00:19:46.907
Oh, fuck.


00:19:49.899 --> 00:19:53.227
One bedroom, high ceilings.
Close to the PATH train.


00:19:53.379 --> 00:19:55.179
Ooh, washer dryer.


00:19:55.339 --> 00:19:57.903
- Plus it's crazy bright.
- Yeah.


00:19:58.058 --> 00:20:00.623
Well, that's morning light.


00:20:00.779 --> 00:20:02.623
I don't want that.


00:20:02.778 --> 00:20:05.627
Wow, that's, like,
your best excuse in two weeks.


00:20:05.778 --> 00:20:07.338
Hello, Koosers.


00:20:07.499 --> 00:20:09.418
- Did you sell that dresser?
- I did not.


00:20:09.578 --> 00:20:11.018
She's not interested
in the apartment, Henry.


00:20:11.178 --> 00:20:12.499
I told you.


00:20:12.658 --> 00:20:14.186
What?


00:20:14.338 --> 00:20:15.942
What do you mean,
"I told you"?


00:20:16.098 --> 00:20:18.782
You've been talking about
moving out for two years.


00:20:18.937 --> 00:20:20.705
You know what?
I'm saving money. Alright?


00:20:20.857 --> 00:20:22.865
I have a very definite plan.


00:20:23.017 --> 00:20:25.221
You mean that "stay at home,
corrode your soul" plan?


00:20:25.377 --> 00:20:27.341
No, no - the plan
where I move to the city


00:20:27.497 --> 00:20:28.981
and I work with
a big designer.


00:20:29.137 --> 00:20:31.265
I've already made
serious contacts.


00:20:31.417 --> 00:20:33.261
From where'?


00:20:33.417 --> 00:20:38.698
Huffman Koos? Well, you know me
and her and Marlon.


00:20:38.856 --> 00:20:41.541
Hey, I'm serious.
We're worried about you.


00:20:41.696 --> 00:20:43.856
OK, thank you.
I got it under control.


00:20:44.016 --> 00:20:45.543
You guys
go worry about yourselves.


00:20:48.496 --> 00:20:50.296
Wow. There she is'


00:20:50.455 --> 00:20:53.663
1 pm. Very impressive.


00:20:53.816 --> 00:20:56.096
So? Did you have fun
last night?


00:20:56.255 --> 00:20:57.935
I'm sure you'd love
a full report.


00:20:58.095 --> 00:21:00.104
You know,
some mothers and daughters


00:21:00.255 --> 00:21:02.895
actually talk about
these things, like friends.


00:21:03.054 --> 00:21:05.182
It's not happening.


00:21:05.335 --> 00:21:09.143
Well, maybe Toby will be
better company than you.


00:21:09.294 --> 00:21:10.702
Hi!


00:21:17.094 --> 00:21:18.818
Try and control yourself.


00:21:23.493 --> 00:21:24.737
Hey, Nina.


00:21:24.893 --> 00:21:27.937
- Morning, Cathy.
- Good morning, Tobias.


00:21:28.093 --> 00:21:30.734
- Uh, you forgot your sweater.
- Thank you.


00:21:30.893 --> 00:21:32.693
Can I get you
some breakfast, honey?


00:21:32.853 --> 00:21:35.057
No, thanks. I'm OK. Thanks.


00:21:36.532 --> 00:21:38.541
Well, I'll give you two
some privacy.


00:21:38.693 --> 00:21:41.420
There you are.


00:21:44.733 --> 00:21:46.533
I can hear you
hovering out there!


00:21:46.692 --> 00:21:48.220
Fine.


00:21:49.532 --> 00:21:51.213
You're looking a little crispy
this morning.


00:21:51.372 --> 00:21:53.413
Oh, thank you.
You can really put 'em away.


00:21:53.572 --> 00:21:56.333
Did I, uh...
Did I pass out?


00:21:56.492 --> 00:21:58.336
Yeah. Mmm, pretty much.


00:21:58.491 --> 00:22:00.695
Sorry about that.


00:22:00.851 --> 00:22:03.372
- No.
- Um...


00:22:04.531 --> 00:22:06.331
Look.
Uh, I was thinking.


00:22:06.491 --> 00:22:10.900
I had a really fun time last night
before passing out, and...


00:22:11.051 --> 00:22:13.179
...I'm supposed to have dinner
with my folks tonight.


00:22:13.331 --> 00:22:16.015
And being as
I'm leaving in two days,


00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:20.731
I thought, you know,
maybe you'd like to join us


00:22:20.890 --> 00:22:23.018
so we could
hang out more.


00:22:23.170 --> 00:22:28.134
Yeah. Dinner with you and
your parents, it...sounds great.


00:22:33.169 --> 00:22:35.373
- Come on, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:37.209 --> 00:22:38.857
Alright. OK.


00:22:39.009 --> 00:22:40.929
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold.


00:22:41.089 --> 00:22:44.778
Toby, it's called
the fast-moving tile game.


00:22:44.929 --> 00:22:46.849
Hold.


00:22:49.689 --> 00:22:51.576
- Let's go, Toby.
- Hold!


00:22:51.728 --> 00:22:54.096
OK. OK.


00:22:54.249 --> 00:22:55.896
Actually,
just go out ahead of me.


00:22:56.048 --> 00:22:57.772
Oh!


00:22:57.928 --> 00:23:00.448
5, the 13. I'm out!


00:23:00.608 --> 00:23:03.215
- What?
- Ah. Yes.


00:23:03.368 --> 00:23:04.928
Now, who's gonna help me
with the dishes?


00:23:05.088 --> 00:23:06.571
I will, Mom. Wait.


00:23:06.728 --> 00:23:08.648
Hang on a sec.
I gotta take this. It's work.


00:23:08.807 --> 00:23:10.367
This is Toby.


00:23:10.527 --> 00:23:12.011
Oh, hello, sir.


00:23:12.167 --> 00:23:13.488
Uh-huh.


00:23:13.647 --> 00:23:14.967
- No, no, it's no problem.
- Yeah.


00:23:15.127 --> 00:23:16.807
I think maybe
I'll go pick up a movie


00:23:16.967 --> 00:23:18.450
in case you want to
watch something later.


00:23:18.607 --> 00:23:21.411
- That sounds fun.
- I'll come with you.


00:23:21.566 --> 00:23:24.174
Keep you company
while Toby does the dishes.


00:23:34.766 --> 00:23:36.129
Look.


00:23:36.286 --> 00:23:39.329
What happened last night
was a mistake.


00:23:39.486 --> 00:23:41.734
- OK?
- No, you're right.


00:23:44.485 --> 00:23:47.650
Relax, OK?
It was nothing.


00:23:47.805 --> 00:23:50.009
And you stopped it.
You're absolved.


00:24:00.324 --> 00:24:01.972
Hello in there?


00:24:02.124 --> 00:24:03.685
Is there anyone in there?


00:24:03.844 --> 00:24:06.768
You just have to
instigate trouble.


00:24:06.924 --> 00:24:09.728
I do not instigate trouble.


00:24:09.884 --> 00:24:11.204
Well, OK.


00:24:11.363 --> 00:24:12.891
Well, then, Why'd you
come to dinner tonight?


00:24:13.043 --> 00:24:14.364
Toby invited me.


00:24:14.523 --> 00:24:16.291
And now that we're
talking about instigators,


00:24:16.443 --> 00:24:18.287
you leaned into me.


00:24:18.443 --> 00:24:20.004
I leaned into you?


00:24:20.163 --> 00:24:22.007
- I leaned... I did not lean.
- Yes, you did.


00:24:22.163 --> 00:24:23.724
- You leaned into me.
- What?!


00:24:23.883 --> 00:24:25.891
Oh... He said, she said.


00:24:27.562 --> 00:24:28.883
He said, she said.


00:24:29.042 --> 00:24:30.722
Where did that come from?


00:24:30.882 --> 00:24:32.802
I have no idea
where that came from.


00:24:39.002 --> 00:24:40.846
I'm not instigating.


00:25:06.280 --> 00:25:07.644
I've been thinking
about getting


00:25:07.800 --> 00:25:09.809
one of those
giant electric snow globes.


00:25:09.960 --> 00:25:13.004
You ever seen one of those?
Really big ones?


00:25:13.160 --> 00:25:15.168
Fantastic.


00:25:15.320 --> 00:25:17.284
Mom?


00:25:17.439 --> 00:25:19.523
We're in here, honey.


00:25:19.679 --> 00:25:22.167
I'm going out.


00:25:22.319 --> 00:25:24.403
Well!


00:25:24.560 --> 00:25:27.080
Well, don't you look nice?


00:25:27.239 --> 00:25:28.767
Thanks.


00:25:28.919 --> 00:25:30.360
So is Toby
taking you somewhere?


00:25:30.519 --> 00:25:33.280
- Uh, yeah.
- OK. OK.


00:25:33.439 --> 00:25:34.803
- Fine.
- Mom!


00:25:34.959 --> 00:25:36.683
Give me some room.


00:25:36.838 --> 00:25:39.119
Fine. Have fun.


00:25:43.038 --> 00:25:44.643
Is she eating with us?


00:25:44.798 --> 00:25:47.679
Toby is taking her out.
She was all dressed up.


00:25:47.838 --> 00:25:49.562
- Toby already left for DC.
- What?


00:25:49.718 --> 00:25:51.125
Yeah, first thing
this morning.


00:25:51.278 --> 00:25:53.122
Some congressman wanted
to be with the delegation


00:25:53.277 --> 00:25:54.838
before they went to China.


00:26:24.316 --> 00:26:27.316
"Left this morning."
Oh, shit!


00:26:39.474 --> 00:26:41.558
- H-hello?
- Mom?


00:26:41.715 --> 00:26:43.723
Listen. I lied earlier.


00:26:43.874 --> 00:26:45.642
I'm not going out with Toby.


00:26:45.794 --> 00:26:47.518
He actually left for Washington
this morning.


00:26:47.674 --> 00:26:50.401
- Oh?
- Yeah.


00:26:50.554 --> 00:26:54.721
I'm meeting Meredith Lovett.
Remember her?


00:26:54.874 --> 00:26:57.197
I didn't tell you because
I know you don't like her.


00:26:57.354 --> 00:27:01.402
Oh, honey, thank you.
Thank you for telling me.


00:27:01.553 --> 00:27:05.361
You know...
You don't have to lie to me.


00:27:05.513 --> 00:27:07.554
I know.


00:27:07.713 --> 00:27:09.437
So where are you going?


00:27:11.033 --> 00:27:14.241
Uh, we're going to the Regal
to see a movie.


00:27:16.232 --> 00:27:17.553
Uh, Mom?


00:27:17.712 --> 00:27:20.232
Thanks...for being so cool


00:27:20.392 --> 00:27:22.640
and letting me come back
and stay and everything.


00:27:22.792 --> 00:27:25.640
I've been feeling really
tossed around lately, so...


00:27:25.791 --> 00:27:29.196
You know.
Thanks for being there.


00:27:30.672 --> 00:27:33.072
OK, well...
I'll see you later for dinner.


00:27:38.031 --> 00:27:39.591
Oh, my...


00:28:16.429 --> 00:28:17.673
Whoa!


00:28:17.829 --> 00:28:19.870
Cathy.


00:28:20.029 --> 00:28:22.232
- What are you...?
- I'm, uh...


00:28:22.389 --> 00:28:24.833
- What are you...
- I'm not, uh... Nothing.


00:28:24.989 --> 00:28:28.513
Paige and I had a fight,
and I spent the night here. So...


00:28:30.428 --> 00:28:32.872
Oh, my God!


00:28:33.028 --> 00:28:34.632
Hey, Nina.


00:28:34.787 --> 00:28:36.228
- What are you...
- Oh, my God!


00:28:36.388 --> 00:28:37.828
Cathy! Slow down.


00:28:37.988 --> 00:28:41.195
Slow down? I can read
an ice bucket, David.


00:28:41.348 --> 00:28:43.389
- Cathy.
- Oh, my God!


00:28:43.547 --> 00:28:46.395
I'm gonna throw up!


00:28:51.506 --> 00:28:54.027
- Jesus, David!
- Paige, listen to me.


00:28:54.187 --> 00:28:56.107
Just tell me how long
it's been going on.


00:28:56.267 --> 00:28:58.427
We kissed. That's it.


00:28:58.587 --> 00:29:01.031
Then what the hell were you
doing in a goddamn motel room?


00:29:01.186 --> 00:29:02.834
This...


00:29:04.586 --> 00:29:07.106
I'm sorry.
The whole thing was wrong.


00:29:07.266 --> 00:29:08.587
But let's be honest.


00:29:08.746 --> 00:29:10.830
Things have not been good
between us for a long time.


00:29:10.985 --> 00:29:12.469
Oh, God, don't do that.


00:29:12.625 --> 00:29:15.025
Don't apologise and then
blame me in the same sentence.


00:29:15.186 --> 00:29:17.194
Come on, Paige.
You're not happy either.


00:29:17.345 --> 00:29:19.746
It's not about
being happy, David!


00:29:19.905 --> 00:29:21.825
Well, then, what is it?


00:29:41.384 --> 00:29:43.152
Jesus, say something already.


00:29:43.304 --> 00:29:45.268
I will say something
when I want.


00:29:45.423 --> 00:29:47.824
You don't get to decide
when I say something. I decide!


00:29:47.984 --> 00:29:50.428
- Then decide already!
- I'll decide.


00:29:50.584 --> 00:29:53.868
You have caused
some serious trouble


00:29:54.024 --> 00:29:55.311
in the past, young lady.


00:29:55.463 --> 00:29:56.871
Don't you
roll your eyes at me.


00:29:57.023 --> 00:29:58.987
I'm sorry, it doesn't work
when you try to play


00:29:59.143 --> 00:30:00.867
the stern father - it looks like
you're pretending.


00:30:01.023 --> 00:30:03.107
Your father is not pretending!
We are furious!


00:30:03.262 --> 00:30:04.670
I'm not pretending.


00:30:04.823 --> 00:30:06.383
David and I,
we like each other.


00:30:06.542 --> 00:30:08.790
- Oh, my God.
- We've always been close.


00:30:08.942 --> 00:30:10.983
It's not like we planned this.
It just happened.


00:30:11.142 --> 00:30:12.747
- You like each other?
- Yeah.


00:30:12.902 --> 00:30:14.223
- Oh, my God.
- Oh, my God!


00:30:14.382 --> 00:30:16.902
I know what this is -
this is some sick revenge


