00:45:06.729 --> 00:45:09.009
he went online and found
a pick-up ultimate frisbee game


00:45:09.168 --> 00:45:10.532
in Paramus.


00:45:10.688 --> 00:45:13.732
Hey, guys! You, uh...
you got room for one more?


00:45:13.888 --> 00:45:15.972
No daylight. No daylight.


00:45:16.128 --> 00:45:20.928
So it was really Jared Kass
and I, and Joel Silver...


00:45:21.088 --> 00:45:22.768
Joel Silver,
the movie producer?


00:45:22.928 --> 00:45:24.172
Yeah. Yeah.


00:45:25.248 --> 00:45:26.731
My mother
had been making herself


00:45:26.887 --> 00:45:28.568
mysteriously unavailable.


00:45:29.727 --> 00:45:31.931
But, as all our neighbours
discovered...


00:45:33.527 --> 00:45:36.692
...she hadn't completely lost sight
of the Christmas spirit.


00:45:41.887 --> 00:45:43.295
Terry!


00:45:43.446 --> 00:45:45.126
Everything was changing.


00:45:45.287 --> 00:45:46.607
Terry!


00:45:46.766 --> 00:45:48.371
No-one even recognised
each other anymore.


00:45:51.206 --> 00:45:53.967
- Smoothie?
- Oh, good God.


00:45:57.046 --> 00:45:59.086
Very good.


00:45:59.246 --> 00:46:01.329
Now kiss the chef.


00:46:13.125 --> 00:46:15.133
Maybe they are
really in love.


00:46:15.285 --> 00:46:16.605
You said it doesn't last.


00:46:16.764 --> 00:46:19.045
You said that the grasses only
wanted the cows for their money.


00:46:19.205 --> 00:46:20.765
Usually that is the case,
but not always.


00:46:20.924 --> 00:46:22.932
- Your dad is pretty cute.
- Don't be gross, OK?


00:46:23.084 --> 00:46:24.928
Just because you haven't gotten
laid in, like, three weeks.


00:46:25.084 --> 00:46:27.048
Perhaps your problem is
more with Nina than your father.


00:46:27.204 --> 00:46:28.971
Oh, is that so, Henry?
Why is that?


00:46:29.124 --> 00:46:30.444
Because maybe
you are jealous,


00:46:30.603 --> 00:46:33.844
because she has travelled
many places and has lived,


00:46:34.004 --> 00:46:36.765
because she takes chances.


00:46:36.923 --> 00:46:38.244
No. You know what?


00:46:38.404 --> 00:46:39.931
You, my friend,
have breathed in


00:46:40.083 --> 00:46:41.927
a little too much
of this cheap pine wax, OK?


00:46:42.083 --> 00:46:44.964
'Cause she's a selfish skank.
And he's selfish too.


00:46:45.123 --> 00:46:47.404
Yeah, but if he
really is happier with her


00:46:47.563 --> 00:46:48.927
and you make him stop,


00:46:49.083 --> 00:46:50.643
then you're the one
who's being selfish.


00:46:52.483 --> 00:46:54.163
That is maybe
the most intelligent thing


00:46:54.322 --> 00:46:55.762
you have ever said.


00:47:11.401 --> 00:47:13.169
Hey.


00:47:13.321 --> 00:47:16.169
What is
Barnyard International?


00:47:16.321 --> 00:47:19.322
Well, um... See those presents
you got at babyGap?


00:47:19.481 --> 00:47:21.609
Instead of giving those
to a baby


00:47:21.760 --> 00:47:23.321
who might already
have lots of clothes,


00:47:23.481 --> 00:47:25.401
why not help a baby
who doesn't have any food?


00:47:25.561 --> 00:47:26.881
They're not for a baby.


00:47:27.040 --> 00:47:28.481
They're for my husband's
new girlfriend.


00:47:30.600 --> 00:47:32.084
Here's some pamphlets.


00:47:34.520 --> 00:47:36.964
"One goat
can provide a family


00:47:37.119 --> 00:47:39.247
"with enough milk
for an entire year."


00:47:41.040 --> 00:47:43.168
It's like the Christmas gift
that keeps giving.


00:47:43.319 --> 00:47:44.879
Yeah. It is.


00:47:45.040 --> 00:47:46.960
That's good. Can I use that?


00:47:47.119 --> 00:47:49.563
Sure.


00:47:56.919 --> 00:47:59.166
Oh, yes! Oh! Oh!


00:48:06.878 --> 00:48:09.878
There are gift receipts inside,
if anyone wants to return them.


00:48:13.518 --> 00:48:15.242
I think after Christmas Eve,


00:48:15.397 --> 00:48:17.842
we should demand
that Paige have dinner with us.


00:48:20.797 --> 00:48:22.477
What are you doing?


00:48:22.637 --> 00:48:24.284
Come here.


00:48:26.437 --> 00:48:28.837
- I have toothpaste in my mouth.
- I don't care.


00:48:34.036 --> 00:48:35.760
Come here.


00:48:46.436 --> 00:48:49.480
OK. Thank you
for dropping me off.


00:48:49.636 --> 00:48:51.677
I got you these.


00:48:56.755 --> 00:48:58.555
Chef's clogs.


00:48:58.715 --> 00:49:00.602
You said after working last night,
your feet hurt, so...


00:49:00.754 --> 00:49:02.434
You're so sweet.


00:49:11.074 --> 00:49:12.918
OK. You're gonna
make me late.


00:49:13.074 --> 00:49:14.874
Whoo!


00:49:24.633 --> 00:49:25.953
- That was fast.
- Yeah.


00:49:26.114 --> 00:49:28.274
Um...


00:49:28.433 --> 00:49:29.917
What?


00:49:32.073 --> 00:49:33.393
Nothing.


00:49:33.552 --> 00:49:34.873
What's up?


00:49:35.033 --> 00:49:36.354
Nothing.


00:49:36.513 --> 00:49:38.117
Come on.
Tell me what's wrong.


00:49:40.032 --> 00:49:42.313
- I...
- I love you, Nina.


00:49:44.272 --> 00:49:47.753
You shit. You suck.
I wanted to say it first.


00:49:49.512 --> 00:49:52.273
Well, now I'm not saying it.
You blew it, buddy.


00:49:54.271 --> 00:49:56.475
I'm just kidding.
I love you too.


00:50:01.391 --> 00:50:04.031
You guys were married
for 28 years.


00:50:04.191 --> 00:50:06.439
If anyone should call,
it should be him.


00:50:06.590 --> 00:50:08.631
- Do you have any perfume?
- No.


00:50:08.790 --> 00:50:11.475
What?! Where are you
even going?


00:50:11.631 --> 00:50:14.031
Well, I read about
a late-evening cabaret show


00:50:14.190 --> 00:50:15.674
that begins at 9:30.


00:50:15.830 --> 00:50:18.078
- I'm taking myself out.
- Cabaret?


00:50:18.231 --> 00:50:20.359
Am I the only one
who's dealing with this?


00:50:20.510 --> 00:50:24.111
I mean, don't you
want to come back home?


00:50:26.069 --> 00:50:27.510
I'm not sure.


00:50:27.670 --> 00:50:30.190
I'm having a good time
for once.


00:50:30.349 --> 00:50:34.277
I'd like to see you
do the same.


00:50:37.869 --> 00:50:39.396
Let's go, guys!
Pick up the pace!


00:50:39.549 --> 00:50:41.229
Hey, Mondo!
Where's my rigatoni? Let's go!


00:50:41.389 --> 00:50:42.873
Bring it up, parmigiana.


00:50:43.029 --> 00:50:44.829
Nina! Plate 27!


00:50:44.988 --> 00:50:46.352
Alright, guys-


00:50:46.508 --> 00:50:48.832
On 24, I got a mahi mahi
and a chicken parmigiana.


00:50:48.988 --> 00:50:50.875
Thanks for sending her to me.
She's a good worker.


00:50:51.028 --> 00:50:52.436
- Well, that's great.
- Chef likes her.


00:50:52.588 --> 00:50:55.753
Haven't seen you and Paige
for a while. It's good to see you.


00:50:55.908 --> 00:50:58.353
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.


00:51:27.266 --> 00:51:30.190
- Done with your appetiser, sir?
- Sorry?


00:51:30.346 --> 00:51:31.874
Done with
your appetiser, sir?


00:51:32.025 --> 00:51:33.989
Yeah. That... Yeah.
That's great. Thanks.


00:51:38.706 --> 00:51:40.233
Hello.


00:51:41.545 --> 00:51:43.073
Hi, Paige.


00:51:45.065 --> 00:51:47.552
Nice move
on the Christmas card.


00:51:47.705 --> 00:51:49.352
Thank you.


00:51:50.385 --> 00:51:53.506
- Dining alone?
- Uh, yeah. I guess.


00:51:54.824 --> 00:51:56.668
So how are you doing?
Is everything...


00:51:56.825 --> 00:51:58.625
Sit down. Don't have to
make this uncomfortable.


00:51:58.784 --> 00:52:00.267
Just...


00:52:02.904 --> 00:52:05.152
Plus, you know
how I hate pleasantries.


00:52:06.664 --> 00:52:08.748
What about you?


00:52:08.903 --> 00:52:10.911
You look happy.


00:52:12.304 --> 00:52:13.864
Things are OK.
You know, I'm...


00:52:14.023 --> 00:52:16.468
If you're happy,
you can say so.


00:52:16.623 --> 00:52:18.390
You don't need
to spare my feelings.


00:52:18.543 --> 00:52:22.427
Just...be genuine,
David, please.


00:52:22.583 --> 00:52:24.187
Please.


00:52:26.583 --> 00:52:28.743
Yes. I'm happy-


00:52:32.142 --> 00:52:33.702
Thank you.


00:52:33.862 --> 00:52:35.422
Yeah.


00:52:36.822 --> 00:52:38.742
Look, I know
there's nothing I can say...


00:52:38.902 --> 00:52:40.310
Then don't try.


00:52:40.461 --> 00:52:42.261
Paige, stop. Please.


00:52:42.421 --> 00:52:44.669
This is exactly
how we got to this.


00:52:46.062 --> 00:52:50.503
OK, not exactly.
It's partly.


00:52:50.661 --> 00:52:53.509
We stopped talking
to each other.


00:52:55.861 --> 00:52:58.425
I used to love who I was
around you.


00:52:58.580 --> 00:53:01.308
What happened to us?


00:53:02.860 --> 00:53:05.348
We used to have fun.
Remember that?


00:53:07.300 --> 00:53:09.821
We used to laugh.
God, you were so funny.


00:53:09.980 --> 00:53:11.627
I'm still funny.


00:53:11.780 --> 00:53:13.864
I'm... Ask them.


00:53:35.819 --> 00:53:37.586
Shelly just fired me!


00:53:37.739 --> 00:53:39.266
Hey, hey.


00:53:39.418 --> 00:53:42.745
- What happened?
- Oh! This is fucking bullshit!


00:53:42.898 --> 00:53:45.462
- What? Why?
- Because he's not an idiot.


00:53:45.618 --> 00:53:48.378
He saw you and Paige, and he
saw me, and he figured it out.


00:53:48.538 --> 00:53:50.861
He said he didn't want
to be in the middle of it.


00:53:51.018 --> 00:53:53.026
And I was good at that job!


00:53:53.177 --> 00:53:55.141
Why...


00:53:55.298 --> 00:53:57.578
Why were you talking to her?


00:53:57.737 --> 00:53:59.417
She came into the restaurant.


00:53:59.576 --> 00:54:02.337
What do you expect me to do?


00:54:02.497 --> 00:54:04.820
I saw you sitting with her,
and I just thought...


00:54:07.377 --> 00:54:08.697
Thought what?


00:54:08.857 --> 00:54:10.624
I don't know.


00:54:13.096 --> 00:54:14.984
You looked normal together.


00:54:22.215 --> 00:54:24.823
Can we please get out of here?


00:54:32.894 --> 00:54:34.258
# I really can't stay


00:54:34.414 --> 00:54:36.214
# But, baby,
it's cold outside


00:54:36.375 --> 00:54:39.255
- # I've got to go away
- # But, baby, it's cold outside


00:54:39.415 --> 00:54:41.019
# This evening has been...


00:54:41.174 --> 00:54:42.702
# Been hoping
that you drop in


00:54:42.854 --> 00:54:44.218
# So very nice


00:54:44.374 --> 00:54:47.418
# I'll hold your hands
They're just like ice


00:54:47.574 --> 00:54:49.374
# My mother
will start to worry... I


00:54:49.534 --> 00:54:51.301
Hi. Mrs Ostroff'?


00:54:51.454 --> 00:54:53.101
We've never met.


00:54:53.254 --> 00:54:55.382
But I'm Ethan.


00:55:00.174 --> 00:55:01.898
You're our leader.
You can't quit!


00:55:02.053 --> 00:55:05.294
Christmas Eve is in, like,
six days. They're counting on us.


00:55:05.453 --> 00:55:09.621
Try and calm down. Calm down.


00:55:09.773 --> 00:55:12.654
Calm down. Order!


00:55:12.812 --> 00:55:14.699
I know you're upset.


00:55:14.853 --> 00:55:18.421
But you're all
dedicated and talented singers.


00:55:19.892 --> 00:55:21.213
Marcus will take over
as leader.


00:55:21.372 --> 00:55:23.696
- What?!
- Marcus?


00:55:23.852 --> 00:55:25.816
- Why are you even doing this?
- Yeah.


00:55:25.971 --> 00:55:29.615
Well, I believe these pamphlets
should explain everything.


00:55:29.772 --> 00:55:32.456
Each cow or goat
will allow its recipient


00:55:32.611 --> 00:55:35.219
independence
and self-sufficiency


00:55:35.371 --> 00:55:37.652
for years to come.


00:55:38.651 --> 00:55:40.855
And that's pretty great,
isn't it?


00:55:42.171 --> 00:55:45.019
Shelly, this has
nothing to do with you.


00:55:45.170 --> 00:55:47.014
No, I know it's complicated.


00:55:47.171 --> 00:55:49.255
No. I understand.


00:55:50.690 --> 00:55:52.458
Thanks for calling back.


00:55:55.290 --> 00:55:56.611
Told you.


00:55:56.770 --> 00:55:58.494
He'll write you
a reference, but...


00:55:58.650 --> 00:56:00.254
Yeah. He doesn't
want to get involved.


00:56:00.409 --> 00:56:03.891
This isn't gonna work.
I need to find another job.


00:56:04.050 --> 00:56:05.730
I can't stay at Meredith's
rent-free.


00:56:05.889 --> 00:56:07.210
I know.


00:56:07.370 --> 00:56:08.690
And I can't stay here,


00:56:08.849 --> 00:56:10.257
across the street
from my parents.


00:56:10.409 --> 00:56:13.170
- I love you. But...
- What the fuck?


00:56:13.329 --> 00:56:16.733
- Ethan?
- What the hell is going on?


00:56:16.889 --> 00:56:19.977
- What are you doing here?
- Ethan? Like, Ethan Ethan?


00:56:20.129 --> 00:56:23.010
- How did you get in here?
- Your mom gave me the keys.


00:56:23.168 --> 00:56:24.816
She told me
to let myself in,


00:56:24.968 --> 00:56:26.496
like you might not
hear the bell.


00:56:26.648 --> 00:56:29.168
Look, Ethan, I'm sorry, but I'm
gonna have to ask you to leave.


00:56:29.328 --> 00:56:32.732
You can ask, but I'm not gonna.
Who is this?


00:56:32.887 --> 00:56:34.775
Ethan, this is David -
David and Paige,


00:56:34.928 --> 00:56:36.892
my parents' best friends
from across the street.


00:56:38.127 --> 00:56:39.687
Why are you telling
your parents' friend


00:56:39.848 --> 00:56:41.168
that you love him?


00:56:41.327 --> 00:56:43.575
The door's open.
What's going on?


00:56:43.727 --> 00:56:45.975
Nina, I need to talk to you.


00:56:46.127 --> 00:56:48.211
Can we go somewhere
for, like, five minutes?


00:56:48.367 --> 00:56:50.047
Ethan!
I think you should leave.


00:56:50.207 --> 00:56:53.055
- Ethan Ethan?
- Yes! Just five minutes!


00:56:53.206 --> 00:56:55.126
She said no, Ethan.


00:56:55.286 --> 00:56:57.534
I'm gonna ask you one more time
to get out of here.


00:56:57.687 --> 00:57:02.335
And if I don't, Pops,
what are you gonna do about it?


00:57:02.486 --> 00:57:03.446
Arggh!


00:57:03.605 --> 00:57:05.013
'Dad!
Hey!


00:57:05.166 --> 00:57:06.006
- David!
- Dad!


00:57:06.166 --> 00:57:07.770
Get off me!


00:57:09.206 --> 00:57:11.454
# Your eyes
are like starlight now


00:57:11.605 --> 00:57:13.133
# To break this spell


00:57:13.285 --> 00:57:16.166
# I'll take your hat
Your hair looks swell... #


00:57:16.325 --> 00:57:18.125
Why don't you go fuck...


00:57:18.285 --> 00:57:21.012
- What?
- Nothing.


00:57:21.164 --> 00:57:22.769
Its OK.


00:57:25.444 --> 00:57:29.645
# Baby,
it's cold outside. #


00:57:39.564 --> 00:57:43.492
Yes, I cheated on you.
And for that, I am deeply sorry.


00:57:43.644 --> 00:57:46.732
But here's the thing.
I'm a sabotager.


00:57:46.883 --> 00:57:50.484
See, any time
anything good happens to me,


00:57:50.643 --> 00:57:52.487
I...I...I just try
and ruin it, you know,


00:57:52.643 --> 00:57:54.203
because I get scared.


00:57:54.363 --> 00:57:58.051
Now, things with us
were really...real.


00:57:58.202 --> 00:58:00.810
But I didn't feel like
I deserved you,


00:58:00.962 --> 00:58:04.563
so I became the sabotager
and, like, destroyed it.


00:58:04.722 --> 00:58:06.686
That's great, Ethan.


00:58:06.842 --> 00:58:08.926
But we can't just go on
and pretend like everything's fine


00:58:09.082 --> 00:58:10.610
because you learned
a new term about yourself.


00:58:10.762 --> 00:58:14.331
And I don't even think
'sabotager' is a word.


00:58:14.482 --> 00:58:16.369
OK. Please allow me
to finish.


00:58:16.522 --> 00:58:19.566
See, I think
you're a sabotager also.


00:58:19.721 --> 00:58:22.765
You totally pushed for us
to get married so you could, like,


00:58:22.921 --> 00:58:25.125
prove to your parents
that, you know,


00:58:25.281 --> 00:58:26.689
you were
this responsible person.


00:58:26.841 --> 00:58:30.682
But simultaneously, you were
just trying to piss them off


00:58:30.840 --> 00:58:32.760
by marrying someone like me.


00:58:32.920 --> 00:58:34.448
I've moved on.


00:58:34.601 --> 00:58:36.924
- OK? David and I...
- David and you...


00:58:37.081 --> 00:58:41.445
He's your parents' best friend.
For Christ's sakes.


00:58:41.600 --> 00:58:44.721
I mean, what... Are you gonna move
here to New Jersey?


00:58:44.880 --> 00:58:47.128
You hate it here.


00:58:49.239 --> 00:58:50.560
We're done.


00:58:50.719 --> 00:58:52.847
OK? Go home.


00:58:53.000 --> 00:58:54.527
I only bought
a one-way ticket.


00:58:57.560 --> 00:58:59.568
Well, I'm not giving up
on us, Nina!


00:58:59.719 --> 00:59:02.000
I love you too much
for that!


00:59:04.759 --> 00:59:06.919
What?


00:59:33.397 --> 00:59:34.957
What are you doing
with my bag?


00:59:35.117 --> 00:59:37.125
Huh? Nothing.
Just getting it some air.


00:59:39.357 --> 00:59:41.518
- Give me my bag.
- No.


00:59:41.677 --> 00:59:43.880
Give me my bag!


00:59:44.037 --> 00:59:47.201
- Eat me, dick slut.
- Give me my bag, Vanessa!


00:59:47.356 --> 00:59:48.839
No, Nina!


00:59:48.996 --> 00:59:50.916
- No!
- Give me my bag!


00:59:51.076 --> 00:59:54.436
- No! No!
- Give it to me!


00:59:54.596 --> 00:59:55.917
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!
- Give it!


00:59:56.076 --> 00:59:57.559
Oh!


01:00:32.633 --> 01:00:34.477
Oh, honey. Uh...


01:00:34.634 --> 01:00:36.314
Honey?


01:00:36.473 --> 01:00:38.393
I'm sorry, Dad.


01:00:38.553 --> 01:00:40.353
Uh...


01:00:45.912 --> 01:00:48.073
Oh...


01:01:01.072 --> 01:01:03.876
Uh, you know, leave it be.
It's a...it's a badge of honour.


01:01:04.031 --> 01:01:05.472
- You sure?
- Yeah.


01:01:05.632 --> 01:01:07.476
There's aloe on the pad
to prevent scarring.


01:01:07.631 --> 01:01:09.115
OK. Um...


01:01:09.271 --> 01:01:14.640
You know, I'm good.
I'm, uh...I'm good.


01:01:16.630 --> 01:01:18.998
I'm so sorry about
all this horrible...


01:01:20.391 --> 01:01:21.918
...stuff.


01:01:23.191 --> 01:01:24.719
I'm just...


01:01:26.071 --> 01:01:27.915
Yeah.


01:01:31.190 --> 01:01:34.878
You know,
my parents were kinda weird.


01:01:35.030 --> 01:01:37.834
That's why I'm, um...


01:01:39.190 --> 01:01:43.794
Sometimes it's really hard
to say everything you want to.


01:01:43.949 --> 01:01:45.509
You know...


01:01:46.989 --> 01:01:51.397
Your father, he loves you.


01:01:52.589 --> 01:01:55.589
Just don't let that
get confused


01:01:55.748 --> 01:01:57.996
with everything
that's happening.


01:02:02.148 --> 01:02:03.511
Life.


01:02:03.668 --> 01:02:04.988
Ooph!


